@host = http://localhost:5246
@json = application/vnd.api+json

### List, paged. Links and a declared meta shape come back alongside the data.
GET {{host}}/contacts?pageNumber=1&pageSize=2
Accept: {{json}}

### One resource, with its company sideloaded into 'included'.
GET {{host}}/contacts/2?include=company
Accept: {{json}}

### Create. No id — the server assigns one and answers 201 with a Location header.
POST {{host}}/contacts
Content-Type: {{json}}

{
  "data": {
    "type": "contacts",
    "attributes": { "firstName": "Edsger", "lastName": "Dijkstra" },
    "relationships": { "company": { "data": { "type": "companies", "id": "8" } } }
  }
}

### Create, rejected: 422 with a JSON Pointer at the offending member.
POST {{host}}/contacts
Content-Type: {{json}}

{
  "data": { "type": "contacts", "attributes": { "lastName": "NoFirstName" } }
}

### Update, the tri-state in one body: lastName is absent so it survives, email is explicitly
### null so it is cleared, and company carries null data so the relationship is emptied.
PATCH {{host}}/contacts/1
Content-Type: {{json}}

{
  "data": {
    "type": "contacts",
    "id": "1",
    "attributes": { "email": null },
    "relationships": { "company": { "data": null } }
  }
}

### Replace the whole tag set. An empty array would remove every member.
PATCH {{host}}/contacts/1
Content-Type: {{json}}

{
  "data": {
    "type": "contacts",
    "id": "1",
    "relationships": { "tags": { "data": [{ "type": "tags", "id": "9" }] } }
  }
}

### Linkage only.
GET {{host}}/contacts/2/relationships/company
Accept: {{json}}

### Repoint the relationship; send "data": null to clear it instead.
PATCH {{host}}/contacts/2/relationships/company
Content-Type: {{json}}

{ "data": { "type": "companies", "id": "8" } }

### The related resource itself, rather than its linkage.
GET {{host}}/contacts/2/company
Accept: {{json}}

### Delete: 204, no body.
DELETE {{host}}/contacts/3

### Missing resource: 404 as a JSON:API error document.
GET {{host}}/contacts/999
Accept: {{json}}
